  "result": "I haven't changed any code yet, because plan mode doesn't allow edits. The plan is in `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\the-help-output-looks-recursive-rose.md`.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` sorts an option's names with `reverse=True`. That lists long names before short ones, so `--help` shows `--name, -n` instead of the usual `-n, --name`.\n\n**Fix:** remove `reverse=True` from that line. Names with the same prefix keep the order they were declared in.\n\n**Not yet confirmed:** this is my reading of the code, and I haven't run `--help` or the tests. Some tests or docs may hard-code the reversed order. If they do, I'll check whether they or my diagnosis is wrong.\n\n**Checking it:** run the formatting, options, basic and commands tests, then look at `--help` for a command with `--name` and `-n`.\n\nThe tools here don't include one for exiting plan mode, so I can't submit the plan for approval. Tell me to go ahead and I'll make the one-line change and run the tests.",
